<%# Tip result (DESIGN.md §4 Hero-result + Stat grid). The headline answer is the grand
    total on a surface card with the 5px coral left rule and a big tabular-nums number;
    the tip amount reads beneath it as the detail line. A stat grid then breaks the bill
    down (bill, tip, total). When the party is split (people > 1) a second, accent-led
    per-person block surfaces the per-person tip and total — the figures the table actually
    needs. `calc:` is a valid Calculators::Tip; result keys are tip_amount / total /
    tip_per_person / total_per_person (ARCHITECTURE.md §4). %>
<% r = calc.result %>
<% split = calc.people > 1 %>
<div class="space-y-4">
  <%# Hero — the grand total, the page's headline answer. %>
  <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
    <div class="flex gap-5 p-7">
      <span class="w-[5px] shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Total to pay</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.04em] tabular-nums text-ink">
          $<%= money_display(r[:total]) %>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
          $<%= money_display(calc.bill) %> bill plus a
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:tip_amount]) %></span>
          tip (<%= percentage_display(calc.tip_percent) %>%).
        </p>

        <%# Bill breakdown — a small data table (DESIGN.md §4 "Data table"): thin rule
            borders, right-aligned tabular-nums money, a hard total row (top border ink). %>
        <table class="mt-6 w-full text-[15px]">
          <tbody>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule">
              <th scope="row" class="py-2 text-left font-medium text-muted">Bill</th>
              <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-ink">$<%= money_display(calc.bill) %></td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-b border-rule">
              <th scope="row" class="py-2 text-left font-medium text-muted">Tip (<%= percentage_display(calc.tip_percent) %>%)</th>
              <td class="py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:tip_amount]) %></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="border-t-2 border-ink py-2 text-left font-bold text-ink">Total</th>
              <td class="border-t-2 border-ink py-2 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-ink">$<%= money_display(r[:total]) %></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Per-person split — only when there is more than one person. Accent-led (the split is
      the positive, useful figure, DESIGN.md §1) using the shared responsive stat grid
      (DESIGN.md §4 "Stat grid", issue #143): `.stat-grid` / `.stat-card` for per-person
      total and per-person tip, each label + value. The shared track sizes each card to the
      canonical min width and flows (two-up on a wide panel, stacking when narrow); the card
      shell + break-words on the value keep a large 6+ digit per-person figure from clipping. %>
  <% if split %>
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)]">
      <div class="p-7">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">
          Split <%= pluralize(calc.people, "way") %>
        </p>
        <dl class="mt-4 stat-grid">
          <div class="stat-card">
            <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Each person pays</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 break-words text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums text-accent">
              $<%= money_display(r[:total_per_person]) %>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-card">
            <dt class="text-xs font-bold text-label">Tip each</dt>
            <dd class="mt-2 break-words text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.03em] tabular-nums text-ink">
              $<%= money_display(r[:tip_per_person]) %>
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
